      "shortNotes": "Electrostatic Potential\n\nV = W/q\u2080 (work per unit positive charge from infinity)\n\nPoint charge: V = kQ/r\n\nDipole axial: V = kp cos\u03b8/r\u00b2; Equatorial: V = 0\n\nRelation: E = \u2212dV/dr\n\nEquipotential Surfaces\n\nSame potential everywhere; no work in moving charge; E \u22a5 surface\n\nPotential Energy\n\nTwo charges: U = kq\u2081q\u2082/r\n\nDipole in field: U = \u2212pE cos\u03b8\n\nCapacitance\n\nC = Q/V; unit Farad (F)\n\nParallel plate: C = \u03b5\u2080A/d\n\nWith dielectric: C = K\u03b5\u2080A/d\n\nSeries: 1/C = 1/C\u2081 + 1/C\u2082 + ...\n\nParallel: C = C\u2081 + C\u2082 + ...\n\nSpherical: C = 4\u03c0\u03b5\u2080R\n\nEnergy Stored\n\nU = \u00bdCV\u00b2 = Q\u00b2/(2C) = \u00bdQV\n\nEnergy density: u = \u00bd\u03b5\u2080E\u00b2",
