      "shortNotes": "Basic Definition \n\nOnly square matrices have determinants\n\n2\u00d72: |A| = ad \u2212 bc\n\n3\u00d73: |A| = a(ei \u2212 fh) \u2212 b(di \u2212 fg) + c(dh \u2212 eg)\n\nProperties \n\nRow/column interchange changes sign\n\nIf two rows/columns identical \u2192 |A| = 0\n\nMultiplying row/column by k \u2192 |A| multiplied by k\n\nAdding multiple of one row/column to another \u2192 no change\n\n|A\u1d40| = |A|\n\n|AB| = |A||B|\n\n|kA| = k\u207f|A| (n = order)\n\nMinors and Cofactors\n\nMinor M\u1d62\u2c7c: determinant after deleting row i, column j\n\nCofactor A\u1d62\u2c7c = (\u22121)^(i+j) M\u1d62\u2c7c\n\nApplications \n\nArea of triangle: \u00bd |determinant of coordinates|\n\nCramer's Rule: Solving linear equations\n\nInverse exists if |A| \u2260 0\n\nCollinearity: If determinant = 0",
