      "shortNotes": "Worker Classification \n\nSelf-employed: Own account workers\n\nCasual wage labourers: Daily wage, no job security\n\nRegular salaried employees: Fixed salary, benefits\n\nEmployment Trends\n\nJobless growth: GDP grows without proportional employment \n\nInformalisation: Over 90% workforce in informal sector \n\nNo social security benefits\n\nSector-wise Employment\n\nPrimary sector: Declining share\n\nSecondary, tertiary: Increasing but not enough\n\nFeminisation of Agriculture\n\nMen migrate to urban areas; women remain in low-productivity agriculture \n\nUnderemployment\n\nWorkers engaged in low-productivity activities despite capacity for more \n\nKey Concepts\n\nWorkforce Participation Rate: % of population in labour force\n\nWorker-Population Ratio: Workers as % of population\n\nCommon confusion: These are different",
