      "shortNotes": "Computer Network Definition\n\nSet of nodes (computers, devices) connected through communication media\n\nPurpose: Communication and resource sharing\n\nBenefits of Networks\n\nFacilitate communication (email, video conferencing)\n\nShare hardware (printer, scanner)\n\nEnable file sharing\n\nShare software\n\nShare information\n\nNetwork Types by Span\n\nPAN: Personal Area Network; ~10 meters\n\nLAN: Local Area Network; building/campus; 10 Mbps to 1 Gbps\n\nMAN: Metropolitan Area Network; city-wide; ~50 km\n\nWAN: Wide Area Network; countries/continents; ~1000 km\n\nNetwork Devices\n\nDevice\tFunction\nModem\tModulator-Demodulator; digital\u2194analog\nEthernet Card\tNetwork Interface Card (NIC)\nRJ45\tConnector for Ethernet cable\nRepeater\tAmplifies weak signals\nHub\tBroadcasts to all ports\nSwitch\tSends to intended port only\nRouter\tConnects networks; finds best route\nGateway\tConnects dissimilar networks (protocol converter)\nWiFi Card\tWireless network connection\nTransmission Media\n\nGuided (Wired): Twisted pair, coaxial, optical fiber\n\nUnguided (Wireless): Radio waves, microwaves, infrared\n\nWireless Media\n\nRadio waves: Omni-directional; through walls; weather-affected\n\nMicrowaves: Satellite communication; up to 100 km; line-of-sight\n\nInfrared: Short-distance (~5 meters); TV remotes, cordless phones",
